A Barbarian's approach to locks is to bash them open, and to traps is to
plow through them.

A Tourist's response is to get someone else to open it for him.

A Ranger has no idea how locks work, but can detect traps well (and gets
'searching' as an intrinsic in-game).

A Rogue can open iron safes in a short period of time, and gets a bonus
to disarming traps and picking locks.

